        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Clip the safety key on every session, and remove it — with the
            machine unplugged — every time you finish.</strong> Those two habits, plus keeping
            children and pets out of the room while the belt runs, prevent the most serious home
            treadmill injuries.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep roughly 6 feet clear behind the belt, never step onto a moving belt, lock folding
            decks properly, and wear proper shoes. Our
